What's new in version 0.4.1
New features
  * Dictionary group page: select several dictionaries (Ctrl/Shift click) and
    move them with Up/Down, Remove or Delete as one block.
  * Reorder dictionaries and groups by dragging; drop a dictionary on a group
    name to move it into that group, which is also the only way to fill a
    group that has no dictionaries yet.
  * Ctrl+` turns all dictionaries of the current group on or off, and
    Alt+1..0 switch between searching only dictionary no. N and searching
    everything except it.  Both can be rebound in the Shortcut page.
  * The preferences dialog has a Cancel button; closing the window or
    pressing Escape discards the changes instead of saving them.
  * Search from a terminal without opening the window: --exact-terminal WORD
    runs an exact-word search over the active group and prints the raw entry,
    --method/-m chooses the search method used at start-up (otherwise the one
    from the previous session is restored), and tools/ebview-format renders
    that output with ANSI colours.

Bug-fix
  * Crash after removing several dictionaries at once.
  * Up/Down and the property panel did nothing on the dictionary group page
    once it allowed multiple selection.
  * The Windows package kept its data in share/ebview while the program looked
    for data/, so the About dialog, the help pages and every bundled default
    file (shortcuts, filters, ending lists, web search engines, GTK settings,
    pixmaps) were unavailable.  The data directory is now probed at run time,
    as on Linux (Windows).
  * Crash when the clipboard held no text, for example after copying an image:
    the window procedure converted an uninitialised pointer, and the clipboard
    memory was unlocked before it had been read (Windows).

Build
  * ENABLE_ASAN option and "build.sh --asan" for an AddressSanitizer build.


What's new in version 0.4.0
New features
  * Search a word directly from the command line: ebview WORD.
  * Press Enter in the text view to search the selected text.
  * Chinese (GB2312) text is now displayed correctly in dictionaries that
    mix it into the EUC-JP stream (e.g. 小学館 中日-日中統合辞書).

Bug-fix
  * Crash when playing the pronunciation on 64-bit Windows.
  * Application icon is now embedded in the executable (Windows).

Build
  * CMake based build for Linux and Windows (MSYS2 UCRT64).
  * Builds with current gcc and CMake; GTK+ 3.0 or later is required.


What's new in version 0.3.4
Bug-fix
  * Search using Kanji character now correctly work.
  * You can input Japanese correctly.



What's new in version 0.3.4
  * Now you specify color to dictionary button and result list.
  * Show dictionary name on tooltip of dictionary button.
  * Menu and shortcuts to Increase/decrease font size.
  * Menu and shortcuts to Expand/Shrink lines.
  * Selection search renewed.
  * Replace special characters undefined iin Unicode.
  * Both Katakana and Hiragana maches interchangeably.
  * When searching dictionary from disk, they are now enabled by default.
  * Now you don't have to push [Update] button when defining dictionary group and web search engines.
  * Now sound will be played using internal routine (Windows).
  * Immediately get clipboard contents (Windows).
  * Config file location changed (Windows).


Bug-fix
  * Garbage shown in Japanese keyword emphasis fixed.
  * Now end tag without start tag will be ignored.
  * Scrolling to the end of contents unintentionally fixed.
  * Aborts when error returned from EB library fixed.



What's new in version 0.3.3
  * Directory group feature.
  * Suppress console message which cause console window to open.
  * Now "normal"  font will be used in headword list.
  * Calculate number of cells from window height.
  * Use BMH method for fulltext search.

Bug-fix
  * Direct editing in dictionary group window may result in segfault.
  * Segfault on next and previous button fixed.
  * Destroying wrong widget in ok_pref() fixed.
  * Freeze on failure of exec() fixed.



What's new in version 0.3.2
  * Drag & Drop enabled in dictionary group window.
  * Compiles with gcc 3.x on Cygwin environment (Windows).
  * Calls ShellExecute() when no external program is specified (Windows).
  * Cache bug fixed (ignore files whose size is zero).
  * Added call to finalize_hookset().
  * Gaiji color is now correct.
  * Now you can use Japanese path name.


What's new in version 0.3.1

  * File Search:
	Searches keyword from file. 
	You can use both text and regular expression as keyword.
  * Japanese stemming fixed.
  * Weblist destroy bug fixed.
  * Has option to suppress image.
  * Tab position is now modifiable.
  * Frame direction is now modifiable.
  * Max search and max items was separated.
  * Search history is saved in file, available next time.
  * Emphasize search word in contents.


